The path parameter has no type annotation, so FastAPI treats it as a string. Adding 1 to a string causes an error.

Corrected code:

from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/users/{user_id}")
def get_user(user_id: int):
    return {"user_id": user_id + 1}

The type annotation also lets FastAPI validate the incoming path parameter.

